{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The graph of a function f on the vertices "},{"code":"0..<n","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": every vertex "},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" has exactly one out-edge,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"v → f(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and a fixed point is a self-loop. Also called a successor graph."}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Following any vertex’s edges eventually repeats, so each weakly connected component holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one cycle, with rooted trees hanging off its vertices (Flajolet and Odlyzko, “Random","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mapping statistics”, EUROCRYPT ’89). ","type":"text"},{"code":"cycleDecomposition()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" finds every cycle and tree in O(n);","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"successor(of:steps:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" answers f^k(v) for any k.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For f given as a closure over a state space too large to store, use ","type":"text"},{"code":"floydCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"brentCycleDetection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which need only ","type":"text"},{"code":"Equatable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" states and O(1) memory.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph stores one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" per vertex, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f(v)"},{"text":". The edge leaving ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":" has position ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"text":", so edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions and edge indices are both the source. For ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"text":" vertex labels, use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<Label, FunctionalGraph>"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph(FunctionalGraph(g)!, labels: g.vertices)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gives a graph ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"g"},{"text":" its labels back.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The graph is immutable: build a new one to change f.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"title":"FunctionalGraph","externalID":"s:16FunctionalGraphs0A5GraphV","remoteSource":{"fileName":"FunctionalGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph.swift#L21"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"FunctionalGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"FunctionalGraphs"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"FunctionalGraph"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/functionalgraphs\/functionalgraph"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/FunctionalGraphs\/FunctionalGraph\/CycleDecomposition"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FunctionalGraphs\/documentation\/Functional